  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      59.53,
      122.13,
      373.54,
      175.31
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2: This clause amends the section 7 of the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects Law, No.1 of 1976 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect of that section as amended is to provide for those who have been enrolled as Associates to the Institute on the day immediately preceding the date of coming into operation of this Act, to be considered as members of the Institute.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      59.53,
      188.13,
      373.54,
      208.31
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3: This clause amends section 12 of the principal enactment and is consequential to the amendment made by the clause 2.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
